        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In Myriad Year Flying Warship, years flow like water Immortal Gu is the core that elevates the Immortal Gu House to rank eight. Its main use had been to produce year Gu that feed Fang Yuan’s year beasts. With a year essence pool in place, the beasts support themselves inside, and he can put the Gu to other work as that House core.",
        "chapters": [
          1795
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "immortal-gu-house-core",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "house_myriad_year_flying_warship",
          "sys_immortal_gu_house"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "feeding": {
    "known": true,
    "food_raw": null,
    "foods": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "It feeds on the water of the River of Time, the same food as year Gu and Spring Autumn Cicada. Once its seal is removed, its Immortal Gu aura leaks and year beasts are lured to attack. Year beasts eat year Gu, and Years Flow Like Water’s endless production makes that lure hundreds or thousands of times stronger than an immortal level year Gu alone. Hei Fan therefore sealed both year Gu and Years Flow Like Water when he set up the true inheritance so no aura leaked.",
        "chapters": [
          1129
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "feeding-and-flaw",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "loc_river_of_time",
          "gu_spring_autumn_cicada",
          "sys_year_beast"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "refinement": {
    "recipes": [],
    "used_in_recipes": [],
    "refinement_materials": [],
    "confirmed_evolutions": [],
    "related_variants": [],
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Hei Fan created Years Flow Like Water. His inspiration came from constantly parallel refining year Gu, and among his Immortal Gu recipes he placed the greatest emphasis on this one. To gather materials he spent the Hei tribe treasury and paid refinement path experts, then failed nine times before succeeding.",
        "chapters": [
          1131
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "hei-fans-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "sys_gu_recipe",
          "fac_hei_tribe"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "When he refined it he failed consecutively and even lost confidence after many failures.",
        "chapters": [
          1169
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "hei-fans-refinement",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ]
  },
  "economy": {
    "canonical_prices": [],
    "price_claims": [
      {
        "text": "After Hei Fan refined Years Flow Like Water, selling mortal level year Gu became his most lucrative business, and within months he was the world’s biggest year Gu vendor. Because of the Gu, immemorial level year beasts once entered his immortal aperture with rank eight battle strength, and the fights inside cost him heavily. He then researched seals that conceal its aura when it is not in use, and he warns any inheritor to use it carefully in battle lest an immemorial year beast be lured into the aperture.",
        "chapters": [
          1132
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "year-gu-trade-and-battle-warning",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      }
    ],
    "game_proposals": []
